WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.780
Hi, this is Presh Talwalkar

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.840
Can you solve this problem which went viral in Japan?

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:13.280
A recent test found that only 60% of Japanese 20 year olds were able to get the correct answer

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:18.080
This is alarming, because it is down from 90%

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.660
- which was the accuracy rate in the 1980s

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.400
Can you figure it out?

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:29.100
To get started, I´m going to over a common mistake

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:34.920
Many people will input this expression into Google or into a calculator

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:41.880
In order to do so, you have to convert the fraction 1/3 into an inline expression

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:46.920
Many people write out the equation in the following form

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:51.480
Now, you will interpret 1/3 as being grouped together

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:56.260
However I will discourage you from writing expressions in this form

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:59.620
It is not clear that the 1/3 should be grouped together -

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:03.920
- because this expression using both the division symbol and the division slash -

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:08.060
- which are the same mathematical symbol of division

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:12.120
Although you want the 1/3 to be grouped together -

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:15.540
- this expression is going to be evaluated by a calculator

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:20.060
- by converting this division symbol into a division slash

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:23.660
This will NOT be equal to the original expression

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:32.040
The calculator is going to look at the  3 divided by 1 divided by 3 as one term and it is going to evaluate it from left to right

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.460
Now a calculator would properly evaluate this 1/3

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:36.580
it´s going to evaluate the 3 divided by 1 first,

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:39.840
- then it is going to divide 3 divided by 3

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:47.320
- and then it is going to do 9 minus 1 plus 1, which will give you the result of 9

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:50.480
If you were to transcribe it on a calculator

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:56.620
- you want to make sure that the fraction of 1/3 maintains grouped together

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:58.980
So instead of writing THIS expression -

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:05.380
- you would like to write an expression which GROUPS  the 1/3 as one group

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:09.660
Now a calculator will properly evaluate this 1/3

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:15.020
- and this whole term: 3/(1/3) in a proper order

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:18.500
3 divided by (1/3) is equal to 9

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:25.280
- and now we have 9 minus 9 plus 1, which give us the correct answer of 1

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:29.980
The problem is a good reminder of the order of operations

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:34.560
These can be remembered by the acronyms PEMDAS or BODMAS

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:38.700
These relates to the order of operations of Parenthesis or Brackets

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.240
- Exponents / Orders

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:42.220
- then Multiplication - Division

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:44.900
- and finally Addition - Subtracton

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:48.480
Another important rule, is that if you have -

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:51.540
- operators of the same precedence -

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:55.240
- you want to evaluate the expressions from left to right

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:57.360
So let's get to that

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:02.920
We have no parentheses or brackets in this expression, we also have no exponents or orders

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:08.040
We do have a division here, which is 3 divided by 1/3

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:11.080
So let's evaluate this first -

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:19.420
3 divided by 1/3 is the same thing as 3 multiplied by the reciprocal of 1/3 which is 3

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:23.460
We now has a multiplication of 3 times 3 -

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:27.160
- which we also evaluate before anything else

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.680
3 times 3 is equal to 9

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:33.320
And now we have an expression with only addition and subtraction

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:37.140
So how do you evaluate this expression? How do you know what to do?

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:41.980
If you have something of the same precidence - addition and subtraction

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:44.880
- you want to evaluate the expression from left to right

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:48.660
So our first evaluation of 9 minus 9 which gives us 0

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:54.140
- then you evaluate the 0 plus 1 which gives us the correct answer of 1

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:56.560
Did you figure it out?

